  "notes": "ALU's official 2025 University Catalog (Version 2) publishes course groupings (core, general education, electives) with total credits, semester count and credits per semester, but does not publish a term-by-term course sequence. Semesters below distribute the catalog's required courses evenly across the catalog-stated 5 semesters x 12 credits, with foundational general education first and catalog-stated prerequisites observed (prereq course placed in an earlier semester). Actual term placement is set with an ALU advisor via the Individual Degree Plan.\nALU awards 'units'; the catalog's tuition schedule prices tuition per SEMESTER CREDIT HOUR, so units are treated as semester credits here.\nCore (30 cr): LGS100, LGS107, LGS103, LGS108, LGS204, LGS206, LGS208, LGS110, LGS200, LGS210. General education (15 cr): HIST160, CMP101, PSY110, ENG160, MAT140. Electives (15 cr): five courses from ACC, BUS, FIN, LGS, CJS.",
